A1. An unhealthy place to go for a vacation. ~ NICARAGUA
A9. What kind of mistake is it to argue with a traffic cop? ~ FATAL
A14. A combination of lenses used in telephotography. ~ ADON
A15. Sea veterans. ~ SALTS
A17. Mystics of the East. ~ MAGI
A18. A lover's promise. ~ VOW
A20. What blue noses do. ~ SNOOP
A22. The nourishment Judge Jr. carries on a Good Will tour. ~ BUN
A23. An obstruction to Republicans on the road to Washington. ~ AL
A24. A word used in referring to the girl-friend. ~ SHE
A26. The narrow way. ~ ALLEY
A28. The person who commits the most crimes in the tabloid. (Abbr.) ~ ED
A29. Negotiations. ~ DEALS
A31. The only kind of things interesting to a big toad in a little puddle. ~ LOCAL
A32. This is over the head of an interior decorator. ~ CEILING
A34. Interesting to those who want to know how the land lays. ~ MAP
A35. A group of States named after the old country. (Abbr.) ~ NE
A36. Mash made from this made the Indians all wet. ~ MAIZE
A37. What it is to start the home fires burning. ~ ARSON
A39. The mark of fistic defeat. ~ MAR
A40. To incite; impel. ~ URGE
A41. What Grandma loved to do. ~ SPOON
A42. No aviator should go up without this. ~ WING
A43. Whom every mother expects to see in the White House. ~ SON
A44. A fabulous old fellow. ~ AESOP
A45. This is something easy. ~ CINCH
A46. Where Lindy got the flying spirit. (Init.) ~ SL
A47. What you like about your best girl. ~ ARM
A48. A feminine attribute almost unheard of these days. ~ MODESTY
A50. To ridicule by imitation. ~ MIMIC
A52. It's hard to get these out of a second-hand car. ~ RIDES
A54. An exclamation. ~ LO
A56. This does its work under a hood. ~ MOTOR
A58. Equality in condition or in value. ~ PAR
A59. To execute. ~ DO
A60. A bad little devil. ~ IMP
A62. A stumbling block in Lover's Lane. ~ RIVAL
A64. A kind of man produced in the early West. ~ BAD
A65. A close relation. ~ NEAR
A67. Covers with wax. ~ CERES
A69. If you're wise this is supposed to be sufficient to you. ~ WORD
A70. A kind of tube. ~ INNER
A71. This brings evidence of oil in Washington. ~ TESTIMONY

D1. These kind of things are usually at sea. ~ NAVAL
D2. This is an object of worship. ~ IDOL
D3. This gives freely—to go-getters. ~ COW
D4. Indefinite article. ~ AN
D5. A word expressing equality; likeness. ~ AS
D6. A tank that goes on joy-rides. ~ GAS
D7. The larger bone of the forearm. ~ ULNA
D8. A coral island. ~ ATOLL
D10. Part of the verb "to be." ~ AM
D11. What many women keep on their husbands. ~ TAB
D12. If you go out with this it is apt to shake you. ~ AGUE
D13. The great American eagle. ~ LINDBERGH
D16. A famous ancient bigamist. ~ SOLOMON
D19. A laminated rock. ~ SHALE
D21. This is a nut. ~ PECAN
D24. To snatch. ~ SEIZE
D25. This fellow is very blue. ~ ELI
D27. A doggy thing to do. ~ YAP
D29. To condescend. ~ DEIGN
D30. These have ginger. ~ SNAPS
D32. A song. ~ CAROL
D33. This gets all tied up. ~ GROOM
D35. Feminine name. ~ NANCY
D36. The man nobody "No's." ~ MUSSOLINI
D38. A deep sleep. ~ SOPOR
D39. Life-savers. ~ MINTS
D41. A money-making race. ~ SEMITIC
D42. What any man is who graduates from the School of Experience. ~ WISER
